   "body": "**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2, cloud/m4q-reliab-opus-review-1189-r1, round 1): APPROVE** — head 333217c6\n\nNo blocking finding. The linked MP reader is equivalent to the Messages one on every write path I traced:\n- **Composer and session**: both get the same `environment.composer` and `environment.topicPages`.\n- **Reply, quote, edit, delete, author \"MP\"**: gated on `composer` only (`replySymbol`, `installMenuActions`, `ReaderReplyFlow`).\n- **Latest post after a reply**: keyed on the page's category, not on how the reader was opened.\n- **Mark unread**: unchanged by this PR; a nil host shows the toast.\n- **Search, offline, AQ**: still keyed on `isPrivateConversation`.\n- **Side effect, wanted**: a topic followed from a linked MP now gets the composer too (it inherited nil before).\n- **Ledger**: none needed; no GAP or changelog row states the old restriction.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. **Low** — `App/SwiftHFRTests/Reader/LinkedPrivateConversationTests.swift:43-50`. The only test that is red before the fix is a source-text check. A gate reintroduced elsewhere (e.g. `guard composer != nil, !model.isPrivateConversation` in `replySymbol`, or in `installMenuActions`) leaves it green. Acceptable given the precedent (`ReaderViewStructureTests`); it would sit better there. The device check on #893 stays the real proof.\n2. **Low** — `LinkedPrivateConversationTests.swift:19` (`aLinkedPrivateConversationHasItsOwnReplyTarget`). Green without the change, as the PR body says: a characterisation test, not a regression test (L01). Keep it, but do not count it as proof.\n3. **Detail** — `docs/lots/LOT-137-reader-links.md:73`. The new legacy pointer cites `21173e77`; AGENTS §2 asks new pointers to cite `87fe0d1c`. Same block there: `HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift:5587-5599`. Add it next to the old range.\n\n**Verified**\n- Diff `19a74ffa..333217c6` read in full, with the call sites of `TopicReaderView(` and `composer`.\n- Source test simulated on both trees: base has the `isPrivateConversation ? nil` branch and lacks the expected line (red); head is the reverse (green).\n- Legacy citation checked at `21173e77` (5482-5494, accurate) and at `87fe0d1c`.\n- `swiftlint lint --strict` (rc 0), `check-lot-deps.py`, `fold.py --check` and `ledger.py guard` all pass.\n- **Not run**: the app tests (Linux cannot build the app). The new test file was read for compile errors against the helper signatures; none found. macOS CI is the arbiter.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
